---
/**
 * SimulatedNote.astro — the SIMULATED honesty panel every demo-flow
 * walkthrough carries (TODO.promotion/06): the CIML reader must never
 * mistake the demo for production data. One component, one wording, so
 * the six walkthroughs can never drift apart on the honesty line.
 */
---

<aside class="simulated-note" role="note" aria-label="Simulated data notice">
  <p class="simulated-note__chip">SIMULATED</p>
  <div class="simulated-note__body">
    <p>
      Everything these walkthroughs show is <strong>simulated</strong>. The demo instance
      at <a href="https://demo.oimlsmart.org">demo.oimlsmart.org</a> runs the real platform
      software, but the cast is fictional by design: the manufacturer ACME Measurement GmbH and
      its LC-500 load-cell line, the Example Issuing Authority (EX1), the Example Test
      Laboratory (ETL), and the BIML officer are demonstration identities, never real
      organizations. The instance re-seeds nightly, so anything entered there is gone by
      morning. No production data, no real applicant, no real certificate appears anywhere on
      these pages; the artifacts are real platform output produced by the fictional cast.
    </p>
  </div>
</aside>

<style>
  .simulated-note {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-amber-warm, #d97706);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--color-amber-warm, #d97706);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-amber-warm, #d97706) 6%, var(--paper));
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .simulated-note__chip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #fff;
    background: var(--color-amber-warm, #d97706);
    border-radius: 3px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.45rem;
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .simulated-note__body p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .simulated-note__body strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .simulated-note__body a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
